Note: Chatbot — a rule-based chat backend that runs out of the box
Note: Run with: epl run examples/official_starters/chatbot/main.epl
Note: Test:     curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/chat -d "{\"message\":\"hello\"}"
Note:
Note: This starter answers with simple rules so it works with zero setup. To use
Note: a real model instead, replace the body of get_reply with a call out to your
Note: AI provider (for example, shell out to `epl ai "<message>"`, or POST to an
Note: Ollama / OpenAI endpoint) and return its text.

Function get_reply takes message
    lowered = lowercase(trim(message))
    If length(lowered) == 0 Then
        Return "Say something and I'll reply!"
    End
    If contains(lowered, "hello") Or contains(lowered, "hi") Then
        Return "Hello there! How can I help you today?"
    End
    If contains(lowered, "help") Then
        Return "I'm a demo bot. Try saying hello, asking the time, or 'bye'."
    End
    If contains(lowered, "time") Then
        Return "The server time is " + now()
    End
    If contains(lowered, "bye") Then
        Return "Goodbye! 👋"
    End
    Return "You said: " + message
End

Create webapp app

Note: ── Health check ──
Route "/api/health" responds with
    Send json Map with status = "ok" and service = "epl-chatbot" and version = "1.0.0"
End

Note: ── Chat  (body: {"message": "..."}) ──
Route "/api/chat" responds with
    data = web_request_data()
    message = data["message"]
    If message == nothing Then
        Send json Map with ok = False and reply = "Message cannot be empty"
    Otherwise
        Send json Map with ok = True and reply = get_reply(message)
    End
End

Say "Chatbot running at http://localhost:8081"
Start app on port 8081
